---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="Get in touch with Thinking About Policing — questions, challenges, corrections and ideas are all welcome."
>
  <article>
    <header class="border-b border-ink-200">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10 py-14 md:py-20">
        <p class="font-sans text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent mb-5">
          Contact
        </p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold text-ink-900 leading-[1.05] tracking-tight">
          Get in touch.
        </h1>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10 py-12 md:py-16">
      <div class="prose-article">
        <p>
          The best way to reach me is by email:
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="mailto:hello@thinkingaboutpolicing.org" class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold">hello@thinkingaboutpolicing.org</a>
        </p>

        <p>
          Questions, challenges, corrections, and different perspectives are all welcome — disagreement done well is how the writing gets better. If you have spotted an error, say so plainly and I will fix it and note the correction.
        </p>

        <p>
          Comments on each article are also open and need no login, so if your point belongs in public, leave it there and others can join in.
        </p>

        <h2>A note on views</h2>

        <p>
          Everything on this site is written in a personal capacity. The views are mine alone and do not represent Sussex Police, any other employer, or any organisation I am associated with. Anything operational or concerning a live policing matter should go through official channels, not this site.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
